    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_a5cf26d0",
      "@type": "AnalogicalMapping",
      "instance_name": "mapping_id_1",
      "label": "The elderly woman is mapped as a person who 'can afford to travel from romania to london still picks your pocket'",
      "description": "The text explicitly attributes the behavior of 'picking your pocket' to the elderly woman, despite her apparent poverty (implied by her traditional attire and setting). The visual of the elderly woman is used to represent the stereotype of a Romanian person who is dishonest or greedy, even when economically disadvantaged. This is an analogical mapping where the visual entity (elderly_woman) is mapped onto the textual entity (text_chunk) to represent the stereotype of a Romanian thief.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
